The facts an agent needs before it can help with this framework, none of which
were in this file: how to install it, where the source is, where the packages are,
and that there is a hosted MCP endpoint it can use as tools instead of scraping.
An assistant asked "add an @imqueue service to this repo" had to infer the install
command from prose on a page it might not have fetched.

`Updated:` is the maximum of the real committed page dates, NOT the build
timestamp — Cloudflare Pages rebuilds on every deploy, so a build date moves when
nothing changed. Without it a cached copy of this index is indistinguishable from
a current one and there is nothing to decide a refetch on.

The closing `%}` keeps its trailing newline; `-%}` would glue "Updated:" onto the
end of the Contact paragraph above.
{%- endcomment %}

